namespace Magma

/-- A member of the class, as the `2` orbit values it takes together with the proof that they name
one. `Magma.tupOK` is three tests: every orbit value is one the group's action allows, the operation
the tuple builds really is invariant, and no excess permutation is an automorphism of it. -/
@[reducible] def tup8R130 : Type := {w : Fin 2 → Fin 8 // Magma.tupOK S8R130.E S8R130.tr S8R130.z S8R130.st S8R130.X w = true}

/-- The class, as a family of magmas indexed by its own membership test. -/
@[implicit_reducible]
def srch8R130 (v : tup8R130) : Magma (Fin 8) :=
  Magma.mk (Magma.transport S8R130.E S8R130.tr v.1)

end Magma

/-! ### The source exhibits

`2` members of the class, chosen by greedy cover so that between them they model all `109` equations
that have a model in the class at all. Each `decide!` is `Magma.tupOK`: the tuple names a member of
the class. It has to be `decide!` rather than `decide` because on `Fin 8` the invariance test alone
is `64` cells times the group, which the elaborator will not walk inside its heartbeat limit; the
kernel still checks it.
-/

